        "original_id": "7ae1c2fd-2988-5eb4-8263-a3b55e247dea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eugene O'Neill, Russell Edson, Gus Edson, Brutus Jones\n- Works: The Emperor Jones\n- Roles: playwright, Nobel laureate in Literature, poet, novelist, writer, illustrator, cartoonist-screenwriter, Pullman porter, emperor\n\nFacts:\n- Eugene Gladstone O'Neill was born on October 16, 1888, and he was an American playwright and Nobel laureate in Literature.\n- The Emperor Jones is a 1920 play by American dramatist Eugene O'Neill.\n- The Emperor Jones tells the story of Brutus Jones, an African American former Pullman porter who kills another black man in a dice game, is jailed, escapes to a small Caribbean island, and sets himself up as emperor.\n- Russell Edson was born in 1935, and he was an American poet, novelist, writer, and illustrator.\n- Russell Edson was the son of cartoonist-screenwriter Gus Edson.\n- Eugene O'Neill died on November 27, 1953.\n- Russell Edson died on April 29, 2014.",
